1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,872
Monday, four in the afternoon.

2
00:00:01,922 --> 00:00:08,328
Malika calls the bank: her papers are verified and her contract is signed, so can her shop start tonight?

3
00:00:08,378 --> 00:00:12,288
Dilnoza has the shop open on her screen, and she cannot switch it on.

4
00:00:12,338 --> 00:00:14,160
Not alone.

5
00:00:14,210 --> 00:00:24,624
In Lesson 17, Dilnoza verified every document and signed the contract, and this lesson is about the last step, the one that lets a shop take real money.

6
00:00:24,674 --> 00:00:28,896
One admin, rushed or bribed, could switch on a shop nobody else looked at.

7
00:00:28,946 --> 00:00:33,384
By the time anyone noticed, it would have taken a week of payments with stolen cards.

8
00:00:33,434 --> 00:00:37,320
So there is no button that lets one admin switch a merchant on.

9
00:00:37,370 --> 00:00:44,544
Under Actions, Dilnoza sees "Request activation", with a short line: ask a second admin to switch the merchant on.

10
00:00:44,594 --> 00:00:46,416
She clicks it.

11
00:00:46,466 --> 00:00:49,152
The page says "Activation requested.

12
00:00:49,202 --> 00:00:55,752
Another admin has to approve it in Approvals." Dilnoza is now the maker: the person who asks.

13
00:00:55,802 --> 00:00:57,624
Nothing changes yet.

14
00:00:57,674 --> 00:01:00,576
Malika's shop stays exactly where it was.

15
00:01:00,626 --> 00:01:03,576
Out of habit, Dilnoza opens Approvals.

16
00:01:03,626 --> 00:01:08,040
Her request is there, with who requested it and when it expires.

17
00:01:08,090 --> 00:01:10,392
But the Approve and Reject buttons are grey.

18
00:01:10,442 --> 00:01:14,424
Hovering over them shows the message: "You made this request.

19
00:01:14,474 --> 00:01:19,056
Another admin has to decide it." The maker can never approve their own request.

20
00:01:19,106 --> 00:01:24,096
The screen does not offer it, and the server refuses it anyway, whatever the screen does.

21
00:01:24,146 --> 00:01:28,176
Ten minutes later, a colleague signs in and opens Approvals.

22
00:01:28,226 --> 00:01:30,768
For this second admin, the buttons are live.

23
00:01:30,818 --> 00:01:35,400
The colleague is the checker: the person who agrees, or refuses.

24
00:01:35,450 --> 00:01:37,272
One click on Approve.

25
00:01:37,322 --> 00:01:43,128
Only now does the merchant become active, and the page says the company is now active.

26
00:01:43,178 --> 00:01:47,952
At that moment the documents are checked again, in case something changed meanwhile.

27
00:01:48,002 --> 00:01:51,936
Had nobody decided in time, the request would have expired.

28
00:01:51,986 --> 00:01:57,528
So a forgotten request cannot be approved months later, when nobody remembers why it was opened.

29
00:01:57,578 --> 00:02:00,864
On the merchant's page, the history shows a new line.

30
00:02:00,914 --> 00:02:06,456
It names the checker as the one who made the move, and the reason says Dilnoza asked.

31
00:02:06,506 --> 00:02:11,040
This is four eyes: two people look at every change that matters.

32
00:02:11,090 --> 00:02:13,248
It is not a rule for merchants only.

33
00:02:13,298 --> 00:02:20,496
Along the top of Approvals wait the other kinds: fee changes, refund windows, and refunds that bank staff start.

34
00:02:20,546 --> 00:02:24,240
Anything that moves money or switches something on needs two people.

35
00:02:24,290 --> 00:02:27,384
One person proposes; another person decides.

36
00:02:27,434 --> 00:02:33,576
Every one of them uses the same screen, the same grey buttons for the maker, and the same history.

37
00:02:33,626 --> 00:02:35,496
Teams often call this red tape.

38
00:02:35,546 --> 00:02:37,368
I think it is the opposite.

39
00:02:37,418 --> 00:02:43,392
With one person, a single mistake or a single bribe is enough to let a bad shop take money.

40
00:02:43,442 --> 00:02:45,264
With two, it is not.

41
00:02:45,314 --> 00:02:53,376
And nobody can pressure Dilnoza into acting alone, because acting alone is not possible, and the history shows both names.

42
00:02:53,426 --> 00:02:58,128
At half past four, Dilnoza calls Malika back: your company is active.

43
00:02:58,178 --> 00:03:01,608
Next: how Malika's website logs in to the bank.
